<title>SWEDEN: Trelleborg acquires Spain's Ibercaucho.</title>
<headline>Trelleborg acquires Spain's Ibercaucho.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish mining and industrial group Trelleborg said on Wednesday it had acquired 85 percent of the shares in Spanish rubber producer Ibercaucho S.A., along with an option to acquire the rest of the company.  </p>
<p>Trelleborg said in a statement the takeover was an extension of the two companies' cooperation within Trelleborg Automotive Iberia S.A., which makes anti-vibration components for the automotive industry.</p>
<p>No financial details of the transaction were reported, but Trelleborg said industrial rubber producer Ibercaucho has an annual turnover of around 300 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1006</p>
